          {
            "tool": "submit_answer",
            "arguments": {
              "answer": "The first book, *The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo*, follows journalist Mikael Blomkvist, who is hired by Henrik Vanger to investigate the 40-year-old disappearance of Henrik's niece, Harriet Vanger, while ostensibly writing a family chronicle. Blomkvist teams up with Lisbeth Salander, a brilliant but troubled hacker, and together they uncover a series of murders committed by members of the Vanger family on their isolated island. The investigation reveals that Harriet was murdered by her uncle Martin Vanger, who had been killing young women for decades. The book ends with Blomkvist clearing his name by exposing corrupt industrialist Hans-Erik Wennerström and Salander defeating her abusive guardian, Nils Bjurman, solidifying their partnership.",
